#### 8. Exception Handling in Tests — `addNullSkuManualCatch` (line 92)

```java
try {
    catalog.add(null, 1);
    fail("should have thrown");
} catch (Exception ex) {
    assertNotNull(ex.getMessage());
}
```

Manual `try/catch/fail` is fragile: catching broad `Exception` can mask unexpected error types; a missing `fail()` call would silently pass.

**Refactor → use `assertThrows`:**
```java
@Test
void addRejectsNullSku() {
    IllegalArgumentException ex = assertThrows(
        IllegalArgumentException.class,
        () -> catalog.add(null, 1));
    assertNotNull(ex.getMessage());
}
```

